compliance-benchmark-audit is the vendor-neutral GRC and technical-benchmark-auditing concepts umbrella.
The GRC body (frameworks, risk, automation, evidence, TPRM, policy, maturity, platform routing) is
sourced from chrishuffman5 (MIT). The technical benchmark-auditing methodology (CIS Benchmark
assessment + NIST SP 800-53 control-family assessment) is genericised and merged from two vahagn
network-security skills (Apache-2.0), attributed per the cloudflare-dns-ops + siem-soar-investigation
mixed-licence precedent. Skill licensed MIT (the primary-source licence); the vahagn-derived material
is methodology and structure, re-authored vendor-neutral, with control IDs referenced for traceability
and no copyrighted benchmark text reproduced.

This skill is a CREATE, not the "extend" the Chunk C disposition recorded. The disposition
(chunk-c-final-dispositions.md lines 92 + 183) assumed compliance-benchmark-audit was a wave-1 adopted
skill and listed it as "0 new + 1 extended". It did not exist on disk. Two skills already carried
dangling cross-references to it (siem-soar-investigation/SKILL.md line 83; merged-skills-registry).
Creating it resolves both pointers with no back-edit, the same pattern as EDR/NDR resolving the SIEM
references in PR #131.

