Customisations applied:
  - Re-authored the agent-style upstreams ("You are a specialist...", "How to Approach Tasks",
    "Technology Routing", "delegate to / route to the appropriate agent") into vault umbrella shape:
    keyword-rich CSO description enumerating the five references and the cross-skill boundaries
    (firewall-audit quartet, aws-networking-audit, wireless-security-audit, siem-soar-investigation,
    identity-access-management, secrets-hygiene, utc-timestamps), four-field vault frontmatter (name,
    description, license MIT, metadata.version 1.0.0 unquoted), skill marker in SKILL.md only.
  - References carry no frontmatter and no skill marker (line 1 is the # Title in each).
  - Upstream names not carried over: chrishuffman5 "security-grc"; vahagn "cis-benchmark-audit" and
    "nist-compliance-assessment" folded as methodology, not as named skills.
  - Upstream metadata stripped: vahagn safety/author/openclaw fields and quoted metadata.version;
    chrishuffman5 quoted metadata.version converted to bare semver.
  - The vahagn benchmark methodology was genericised: the network-device "Management / Control / Data
    Plane" structure is retained as the example for network-device benchmarks but framed as one case of
    a general Pass/Fail/N-A assessment that also covers OS, cloud, Kubernetes, and database benchmarks.
  - Em-dash (U+2014) and en-dash (U+2013) glyphs: zero occurrences. ASCII "->" for arrows and flows;
    commas, colons, semicolons, and parentheses for dash-style pauses; ASCII hyphen only in numeric
    ranges and compound words.
  - British/Pacific English applied: organisation, prioritise, minimise, centralise, behaviour,
    licence (noun), defence, categorisation, authorisation. Proper nouns left intact (NIST, FIPS,
    FedRAMP, CMMC, POA&M, framework control IDs).

Boundary notes:
  compliance-benchmark-audit = vendor-neutral GRC (governance, risk, compliance) plus technical
  benchmark/control-family auditing methodology. It does NOT own: device-level CIS hardening of a
  specific firewall (firewall-audit quartet); cloud security posture / CSPM / CNAPP scanning
  (cloud-security-posture family, not yet in this vault, referenced in prose only, no dangling link);
  vulnerability scoring and remediation programmes (vulnerability-management family, not yet in this
  vault, prose only); the mechanics of the controls themselves (identity-access-management,
  siem-soar-investigation, infrastructure skills). The five GRC platforms (Vanta, Drata, OneTrust,
  ServiceNow GRC, Archer) are skipped/refer-only per the generic-only disposition; this umbrella names
  them as routing context only.

